[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Authorization and State-Write Boundary[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe new country scaffold introduces no provider-facing RPC that writes official source, legal approval, connector, release or enforcement state. Existing Faz 8-A tests remain the authoritative negative test set for provider capability profile writes: provider-owned declaration paths cannot override system enforcement, approval ledger validity is required, and stale writes are rejected. The country deployment policy is server-side and only narrows existing transition gates.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe generic `approval_ledger` table is an append-only data model: it has event rows and no update/delete policy path in the scaffold. No owner/admin mutation procedure was added in this checkpoint. A ledger row alone is intentionally not treated as activation evidence by `countryActivationPreflight`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe detailed role/RPC boundary and the executed negative test command are recorded in `DE_BERLIN_AUTHORIZATION_BOUNDARY_EVIDENCE.md`. TiDB/MySQL RLS is not available in this deployment, so no database RLS test is claimed; the evidence instead records the application-layer server/tRPC boundary and the absence of a new country-scoped write RPC.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Environment and Working Tree[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mManaged TiDB migration testing is **not** evidence of production deployment. Physical production/staging/development isolation and a production change record are unavailable; status remains `ENVIRONMENT_SEPARATION_UNVERIFIED`. The package records only test/staging-schema application. Git diff and working-tree evidence are captured in the final package manifest; no private environment value, connection string, credential or user data is included.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## TypeScript Memory Evidence[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Check | Result | Interpretation |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| `NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=512 pnpm exec tsc --noEmit --skipLibCheck` | Node heap OOM / exit 134 | Not a PASS; a 512 MB-only CI worker is a build blocker |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=1792 pnpm exec tsc --noEmit --skipLibCheck` | PASS | No TypeScript diagnostic; controlled higher-heap verification |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Standard production bundle `pnpm build` | PASS | Backend bundle completed; does not prove a 512 MB typecheck budget |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe recursive process measurement recorded a **612,416 KiB** peak RSS for the 512 MB run. Node’s own final V8 trace showed 509.5 MB used against a 524.2 MB heap limit immediately before abort. This sandbox has no approved CI memory-budget record; therefore the minimum safe CI budget is **not certified**. The only reproducible successful command evidenced here is:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mNODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=1792 pnpm exec tsc --noEmit --skipLibCheck[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe 512 MB command must remain an external CI-capacity gate until a measured, approved build-budget decision exists. The final full regression after the legal-locale contract addition is **125 test files / 732 tests PASS**; targeted Germany/Türkiye policy evidence is **4 files / 20 tests PASS**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Test Discovery Integrity Correction[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe read-only export package intentionally carries copies of selected test files as audit evidence. Vitest’s default repository-wide discovery could treat those incomplete copies as runnable tests. `vitest.config.ts` now explicitly includes every source test under `tests/**/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx}` and excludes `exports/**`, `dist/**`, and `node_modules/**`. `tsconfig.json` likewise excludes `exports`, so incomplete audit copies cannot create artificial TypeScript errors. A file-system audit confirmed that the source `tests/` directory contains 125 matching test/spec files, and the subsequent full regression ran all 125. This correction prevents an export artefact from changing test execution; it does not delete, skip, or weaken any project test.[m
